{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the retained receipt that carries the deterministic joint-change case (CheckRun eb27767ba74043ada1911d66fc9c4188: completed, tests_passed, exit 0, 18 parsed observations, 0 parse errors), superseding the source-only account for @joint_apply_order with observed operands. Index 16 shows: after a JointImplicit learner-add the tracker is joint (joint_after_first_joint_change=true) with auto_leave=true and voters unchanged [1,2,3]; a second joint-entering change while joint is rejected with exactly 'config is already joint'; applying the leave-joint change returns the tracker to non-joint (joint_after_leave=false); and the same change is then accepted with no panic (third_change_panic empty), ending with learners [4,5]. That is the contract's ordering requirement made concrete, and it explains the earlier harness panic as the harness applying a change whose precondition it had not satisfied - the target's documented reaction to an invalid change - so the defect claim for this investigation is refuted for the histories exercised, not carried forward as a suspicion. Index 17 confirms the sweep is unchanged by the added case (elections=470, ordinary proposals=461, conf_change_proposals=262, restarts=429, unapplied_conf_change_states=48, stalled_states=0, violations=0) and that its holds-only limits still apply. Kept explicit as remaining work: the deterministic case establishes the precondition but not reachability, so whether a permitted history can force an in-order application to meet a joint-entering change before its leave - a leader that never applied the joint change while leading, or a leadership change after which no one pursues the leave - still needs the reachability variant of the discriminator, which this submission does not include; the case also says nothing about other cluster sizes or about changes arriving in different terms.\"}"}}
